      "roc_auc": 0.999945,
      "accuracy": 0.999802,
      "majority_baseline": 0.994638
    },
    "inflation_delta_pr_auc": 0.019717,
    "explanation": "A random pair-level split allows pairs from the same patient entity to appear in both training and test partitions. The classifier memorizes specific demographic combinations (e.g. rare Pakistani family names or specific birth dates), falsely inflating PR-AUC. Under our honest entity-grouped temporal split, test entities are prospective patients registered after April 2022 who were never seen during training, guaranteeing a truthful assessment of real-world clinical deduplication capability."
  },
